# Local WoT graph and relay sync

## Graph heap is runtime truth

The Trust Graph heap (`src/graph/trust` `Graph`) is the **single in-memory
point of truth** for trust data. Do not keep event lists, twitterId↔npub maps,
or `xIdentities` / `xPosts` RAM catalogs beside it. If those lists are needed
in memory, store them **on the Graph instance** (same as `bindIdentity`).
Operational lists may live outside the Graph: active relays, outbox, vault,
and **current user / panel director** (`PanelSessionController`). That
session pattern is operational, not heap data.

- **Write:** update IndexedDB **and** the heap in the same pass
  (`GraphManager.applyRecord`, identity bind, chrome on Graph).
- **Read:** Graph first; on miss, IndexedDB then fill the heap.
- [`graphManager.ts`](../../src/background/graphManager.ts) is the facade
  [`backend.ts`](../../src/background/backend.ts) uses. Return one payload
  (e.g. trusted edges + matching `xIdentities`) so UI/content does not make
  N follow-up RPCs.
- Scores: `IndexResolver` + `pathStrategyJson` (timeline and Path View).
  Panel / Graph View: `Graph.out` / `Graph.in` / neighborhood, then decorate
  from chrome caches on the Graph.
- Details: [docs/architecture.md § Trust graph heap](../../docs/architecture.md#trust-graph-heap-runtime-source-of-truth).

## Trust folder: ask, do not compensate

[`src/graph/trust`](../../src/graph/trust) is locked. If Graph, IndexResolver,
or `pathStrategyJson` cannot do what the product needs, **ask permission**
and state the missing capability. Do **not** write a workaround graph, a
second resolver, or extra hop logic outside this folder.

**Do not invent a Trust Graph resolver outside `src/graph/trust`.**
`IndexResolver` is the walk. It is highly complex on purpose. When hops or
scores look odd, the user cannot fix a custom resolver sitting outside Trust.
`query.ts` may map `Score[]` to DTOs. Do not grow `identity-index-resolver.ts`
or add another `IResolveStrategy`. Rating overlay (`ratings/`) must not clone
the IndexResolver walk.

Wrappers that are allowed without Trust edits: `src/graph/graph.ts`,
`adapter.ts`, `query.ts`, `ratings/` (overlay only), and GraphManager — attach
identity / chrome caches on the Graph instance; compose one round-trip
payloads.

## Product rules

- Trust results are subjective evidence for the local root, context, and bounds — never an objective or universal score.
- Preserve direct evidence, paths, source event IDs, graph version, and truncation state in query results.
- Kind `32009` only for trust statements; kind `32014` for ratings (never hops). Optional `l` labels augment either with human clarification and are not hops.
- Scope (`s`) is **not** part of graph slot identity or resolve. Handle it at publish, relay filter, and ingest eligibility. See [docs/architecture.md § Scope policy](../../docs/architecture.md#scope-policy-attentionx-on-xcom).

## Hot path vs durable state

- Timeline CPU first: scroll queries must stay in-memory heap lookups. A slow graph rebuild or per-cell RPC makes the feed unresponsive; if that happens, nothing else matters. See `docs/architecture.md` § Timeline CPU and responsiveness.
- Durable source of truth: current winning signed events (+ `xIdentities` / `xPosts`) in IndexedDB — not a full history of replaced addressable slots.
- Hot path: Graph heap via GraphManager answering `QUERY_TRUST` / `QUERY_TRUST_BATCH` and `QUERY_RATING` / `QUERY_RATING_BATCH` without IndexedDB per lookup.
- Prefer a personal graph snapshot in IndexedDB for fast rehydrate after SW restart (see `docs/architecture.md` § Hot trust graph) — do not rely on immortal SW memory alone.
- Validate and reduce on ingest; avoid rebuilding the graph by re-validating every stored event on SW wake.
- Do not invent content-script `GRAPH_KEEPALIVE` or offscreen-document graph holders unless implementing that design deliberately.

## Bounds

- Sync and traversal are depth/fan-out/author/event bounded; follow only active positive `p` edges for expansion.
- `p` subjects are traversable; X account/post `i` subjects are terminal evidence.
- Advance relay cursors after EOSE with an overlap window; dedupe by event ID across relays.
- Kind `32009` relay pulls on x.com must cover **`#s=x.com` and empty-scope** events (user trusts omit `s`; post trusts use `x.com`). See `src/relay/filters.ts` and architecture scope policy.
- Product Graph snapshot, neighborhood, and Path trust queries walk `c=identity`. Post rating overlays query empty context. Traversal still follows only Trust (`1`) `p` hops; Neutral (`0`) edges may be visualized.

## What not to use

- `chrome.storage.local` / `session` for the large personal WoT.
- Per-tab content-script graph caches as the source of truth.
- Sidecar trust-event or identity lists on Backend / RuntimeContext.
